body:
FEATURE SPEC: Sticky Question Position Tracker
Based on T25 component design (annotated)

Filed by: GD
For: GA implementation in exam.html

WHY
WCAG 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships) + ADHD protocol: after a wrong answer, Kai loses scroll orientation.
A persistent position indicator prevents the "how many left?" cognitive search mid-exam.

HTML
Add immediately above questionsContainer in exam.html:
  <div id="questionTracker" style="display:none" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Question position"></div>

aria-live="polite": announces position to screen readers on change without interrupting focus.

CSS (add in exam.html <style> block)
  #questionTracker {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 100;
    padding: 6px 16px;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);     /* 14px — readable in peripheral vision */
    color: var(--text-secondary);  /* subdued, ambient info */
    background: var(--bg-page);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);
    text-align: right;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    #questionTracker { padding: 4px 12px; }
  }

JS (add in loadExam(), after renderQuestions() call)
  var tracker = document.getElementById('questionTracker');
  var qEls = questionsContainer.querySelectorAll('.question-block');
  if (qEls.length > 1) {
    tracker.textContent = 'Q1 of ' + qEls.length;
    tracker.style.display = '';
    var io = new IntersectionObserver(function(entries) {
      entries.forEach(function(e) {
        if (e.isIntersecting) {
          var idx = Array.prototype.indexOf.call(qEls, e.target) + 1;
          tracker.textContent = 'Q' + idx + ' of ' + qEls.length;
        }
      });
    }, { rootMargin: '-20% 0px -60% 0px', threshold: 0 });
    qEls.forEach(function(el) { io.observe(el); });
  }
  // Hide tracker after exam is graded (scorecard is shown)
  // Add to gradeExam(): tracker.style.display = 'none';

EDGE CASES
- Single question exam (qEls.length === 1): do NOT show tracker (already handled by qEls.length > 1 guard)
- Picker mode (no questions): questionsContainer is empty, qEls.length === 0, tracker stays hidden
- Exam graded: tracker hidden after gradeExam() runs (add tracker.style.display = 'none' in gradeExam)
- Scroll to top: tracker shows Q1 of N correctly

DESIGN NOTES
- text-align: right -- puts number out of question reading path, stays in peripheral vision
- border-bottom subtle -- separates tracker from content without a heavy border
- z-index 100 -- above question cards, below any future modal (use z-index 200+ for modals)
- No animation on update -- instant text change reads as reference, not notification

ACCEPT CRITERIA
[x] Tracker shows 'Q1 of N' when exam loads (N > 1)
[x] Updates as Kai scrolls through questions
[x] Hidden in picker mode (no exam loaded)
[x] Hidden when exam has only 1 question
[x] Hidden after gradeExam() runs
[x] Announced to screen readers on change (aria-live polite)
[x] Sticks to top of viewport while scrolling
[x] Does not overlap question content (sticky, not fixed)
